 "requested_at": "2026-11-13T20:08:41.948523Z",
 "text": "Under the *Residential Tenancies Act, 2006* (RTA), a landlord cannot require or take a tenant's notice of termination at the time the lease is entered into. Subsection 37(5) specifically provides that a notice of termination given by a tenant is void if it is given at the time the tenancy agreement is entered into or as a condition of entering into the tenancy agreement. \n\nAdditionally, under section 5 of the RTA, any term or condition in a tenancy agreement that is inconsistent with the Act is void.\n\nVerdict: not enforceable\nSection: 37(5)",
